module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.an_asset_reference_extractor_narrower_than_the_html_it_reads

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { FoundAtAmbiguous, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data an_asset_reference_extractor_narrower_than_the_html_it_reads: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "an_asset_reference_extractor_narrower_than_the_html_it_reads" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: FoundAtAmbiguous },

  receipts: [
    "**a reader of a vendor page accepted only the spelling this repository's HTML WRITER emits (a space, then `src=`, then a double quote), so every other valid attribute form produced an empty result that the receipt then rendered as a fact about the page** (INVALID STATE: `refs=0` meaning 'the parser did not recognise it' while the line and the conclusion read 'no page named a script'. HARM: the read the whole mtcollins1 status-label chain depends on returned nothing, and the empty receipt could not distinguish a login or redirect stub, a loader page, a single-quoted, unquoted, uppercase or newline-led reference, and a script-free landing page; the next step was a guess about the controller when the deficit was in this module). DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the first extractor's own comment recorded the limit ('a script written with single quotes or with a newline before the attribute is NOT collected') and declared the empty receipt honest; it was not, because the empty case and the unread case printed identically.",

  "RECEIPT 2026-11-06, fleet-converge run 42042565485 (mtcollins1_fan_observe, srv1, main d232a85d): both candidate pages answered 200 with `refs=0`, no asset was fetched, no excerpt exists. Whether the pages carry scripts in an unread form is UNMEASURED at the time of filing; the page_shape line added with the fix is what answers it on the next read. The finding stands without that answer: an extractor narrower than the grammar it reads, whose empty output is reported as a property of the input, is a defect whatever the page turns out to contain.",

  "RUNG FOUND AT: OUTSIDE THE LADDER for the unread forms (the result was wrong-by-omission and reported as true). CEILING: a decidable class. The attribute forms are the WHATWG HTML tokenizer's (HTML Living Standard 13.2.5), which is fully specified, so the reader can be total over them; the reader is tag-aware (start-tag attributes only; text, comments, end tags and script/style bodies are not read), and the typed conclusion ScriptTagsWithoutDerivedReference makes a script-bearing page with no derived reference visible. The fix reads whitespace-led, ASCII-case-folded `src` and `href` with double-quoted, single-quoted and unquoted values, and when a 200 page carries `<script` tags while no reference was derived the conclusion says so instead of 'no page named a script'. Executed evidence: one witness per attribute form plus a longer-name and unterminated-quote negative, in test.claim.machine_intake.mtcollins1_ui_status_asset_observation_witness. READING HOME: the reader lives in extdeps.whatwg.html_attribute_tokenization (WHATWG 13.2.5 state names kept) and this module consumes it. SECOND IMPLEMENTATION OF ONE RULE (gunbc.design_argument::root_generalization root generalization): extdeps.languages.html parse_attrs_with splits attribute text on the double quote only, so it reads the same grammar narrower. Answer: SHOULD BE GENERALIZED, NOT NOW, because changing it alters the ingest of every consumer of that shared parser and must not ride in the PR that unblocks the UI read. TRIGGER: #15960 merged; a follow-up PR makes html parse_attrs_with consume html_attribute_tokenization and deletes its own double-quote splitting; owner wise-wolf-367; swept by merry-fox-82. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER for the extractor itself: the unmodeled residue named in the module (character references, CDATA in foreign content, `<!-->`, duplicate attributes) matters to a consumer; the witnesses stay as regression controls (gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder (dissolution on climb))",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
